+# CHECK-R48C — Q6_K mat-vec x-fold + activation hoist (Fable 5.1 LOW, independent checker)
+
+Worktree `C:/ArifiLabs/cache/r48c-q6k-wt`, branch `lane-236/r48c-q6k-matvec-2026-09-14`, HEAD `0e1660a39`
+(= maker draft `647eb6ac9` + report/localisation commit), base `9ff4644b1`. Tree clean apart from the
+checker prompt and three new checker receipts (`r48c-evidence/40-*`, `41-*`, `42-*`, untracked).
+
+## LENS
+
+Is the Q6_K change correct, honest, and worth keeping at default ON. Six sub-questions from the brief:
+(1) correctness and the localisation of the intermittent all-zero at 248320x5120 n=1; (2) planted red;
+(3) pairing rows, controls, protected-win survival; (4) MMVQ route diagnostic; (5) the -32 fold's
+float-reordering tolerance; (6) report honesty, registry, trailers.
+
+## FINDINGS
+
+1. **The "pre-existing" claim is now SETTLED, not just argued — by a receipt the maker did not take.**
+   `r48c-evidence/42-check-upstream-shader-q6k-248320-60.txt`: with BOTH ArifiLabs constants off
+   (`GGML_VK_Q6K_DIRECT_SCALES=0 GGML_ARIFI_Q6K_XFOLD=0`, i.e. upstream's LDS-staging shader path byte
+   for byte), the 248320x5120 n=1 filter fails **3/60** (ERR 1.000000000, 0.997189778, 1.000000000).
+   That is the same ~5% rate and the same all-zero signature as the maker's 7/140. The defect therefore
+   predates lane-236 AND lane-209 in the shader. Report §10.2 (the "shader cannot cause it" table) is
+   correct as code reading, and this receipt is the empirical proof it lacked. Fix: cite this receipt in
+   §10.1 / §10.7 and in the HQ re-open against the Vulkan sync lane.
+   Counter-receipt in the same session, `40-check-sx8-zsplit-60.txt`: SX8 at the identical shape and
+   identical z-split dispatch (the only other 248320 eval row) is **0/60**. At 5% that is p≈0.046, so
+   the trigger is not the z-split geometry alone — something on the Q6_K dmmv path (host side: pipeline
+   selection, the ~1 GiB src0 upload/placement, or the `ggml_vk_synchronize` bookkeeping the maker names)
+   is involved. This narrows the maker's lead but does not contradict it; it must be stated so HQ does
+   not re-open against "the z-split" generically.
+
+2. **§10.3 over-claims "ERR exactly 1.0 on every failure" and "rules out arithmetic for good".**
+   The lane's own receipts hold two non-1.0 failures: HQ's 0.996978715 (`11-mulmat-xfold-off.txt:2573`),
+   the first attempt's 0.055269269 (`30-failrate-both-arms.txt`), and this check's 0.997189778. An NMSE of
+   0.997 or 0.055 is a partially-written or partially-stale destination, not all-zero. That is still a
+   synchronisation/readback signature, not arithmetic, and it still appears on the pure-upstream path
+   (finding 1), so the verdict stands. Fix: reword §10.3 to "all-zero or partially-stale destination
+   (ERR 1.0, 0.997, 0.055 observed)", drop "every one of the six failures".
+
+3. **The f16-src1 correctness rows are declined, never executed — the `f16_f32` Q6_K pipeline is
+   uncovered while §4 and the test comment claim coverage.** `10-mulmat-xfold-on.txt` and
+   `12-mulmat-q6k-mmvq-route.txt`: all 8 `type_a=q6_K,type_b=f16` rows read `not supported [CPU]`
+   (0 OK). The registration at `ggml-vulkan.cpp:7166` takes the new constant and has no test. Fix: either
+   state the gap in §8 and in the test comment (`tests/test-backend-ops.cpp` ~:10745, "F16 src1 is
+   included because…"), or drop the rows. Risk is low: at every `NUM_COLS` the f16 pipeline shares the
+   GLSL body and `B_TYPE` is converted through `FLOAT_TYPE` before arithmetic, but "covered" is false.
+
+4. **The protected win's own quality gate was not re-run on the new shader before this check.**
+   `protected-wins.json` entry `vulkan-q6k-matvec-direct-scales` gates on "0 FAIL on BOTH arms; plus
+   byte-identical llama-server output between the arms". HQ's receipts 10/11 both ran DIRECT_SCALES=1
+   only. This check ran the missing half: `41-check-direct-scales-0-both-xfold.txt` —
+   `GGML_VK_Q6K_DIRECT_SCALES=0` at XFOLD=1 **43/43** and XFOLD=0 **43/43** (stderr receipts
+   "direct-scales: OFF" / "activation-hoist+xfold: ON|OFF" both present). The `i < num_blocks_per_row`
+   guard that exists only for that arm is therefore exercised and green. NOT run here (needs a model):
+   the serve-level bit-identity between the two DIRECT_SCALES arms at fixed XFOLD=1, which the report §4
+   argues by construction (the fold sits strictly after `sc0..sc6`/`d` are in registers, identical in
+   both arms). Sound argument; the entry's gate text still requires the measurement. Named as the gate.
+
+5. **Report acceptance rule 1 (§6, "ship if ≥ +5% at n=1 on both FFN shapes") is NOT met and the
+   report must say so rather than let "keep" rest on it.** `32-paired-r48cq6k.txt`: n=1 ffn-down
+   +5.61%, ffn-gate-up +3.69%, embd-out −0.21%, legacy4096 +1.20%. The keep verdict is legitimately
+   carried by rule 2 (veto: no q6_K row below −3%, worst −2.97% legacy4096 n=4 and −2.91% n=8) plus the
+   n=6 result (+38.0% embd-out, +27.5% ffn-down, +26.3% ffn-gate-up, 3/3 rounds — an arm-A dip at
+   `NUM_COLS==6`, A = 31.1 GB/s at n=6 against 67.2 at n=5 and 53.5 at n=7, which arm B removes).
+   Fix: registry row and §6 must record "rule 1 not met on gate-up; kept on no-harm + n=6".
+
+6. **`docs/OPTIONS-REGISTRY.md:42-43` still read "UNMEASURED at registration. No speed figure exists and
+   none may be quoted"** after the pairing exists (`32-paired-r48cq6k.txt`, `32-paired-r48cq6kroute.txt`).
+   §8.7 of the report itself says the rows must be re-written before the lane is called done. Fix: replace
+   with the measured row: n=1..5,7,8 wash (−3.0..+5.6%), n=6 +26..+38%, no row below −3%, 3 quiet
+   interleaved rounds, same binary env-flipped; and for `GGML_ARIFI_Q6K_MMVQ`: n≤4 wash/+5%, n≥5
+   −46..−143% (collapse), correctness 43/43 — DIAGNOSTIC, default stays f32.
+
+7. **Fold tolerance argument is sound; sweep coverage of it is adequate with one caveat.**
+   The fold is live only at `NUM_COLS<=3` and `XFOLD=1`. Reordering: `Σ b·(u−32)` becomes `Σ b·u − 32·Σb`
+   in fp32 with |u|≤63, 4-term sums, activation |b|≤1 in the test; worst-case cancellation error
+   ~1e-6 relative on a per-sub-block partial, then scaled by `sc`·`d` exactly as before. Against the
+   MUL_MAT NMSE gate 5e-4 that is 2-3 orders of margin. Covered by receipts at k=5120 and k=17408, n=1..3,
+   plus tails m=17407/7 (10-mulmat-xfold-on: 1688/1688). Caveat: `FLOAT_TYPE=float` for all dmmv
+   pipelines is CHECKED by the maker at `vulkan-shaders-gen.cpp:846`; I did not re-derive it. No fix needed.
+
+## CHECKED
+
+| item | result | receipt |
+|---|---|---|
+| xfold-on full sweep | 1688/1688 | `10-mulmat-xfold-on.txt`, rc 0 |
+| xfold-off full sweep | 1687/1688, only 248320x5120 n=1, ERR 0.996978715 | `11-*.txt:2573`, rc 1 |
+| MMVQ route correctness | 43/43 (8 f16 rows declined) | `12-*.txt`, rc 0 |
+| planted red | applies (`20-red-build` rc 0), 0/8 in BOTH arms with ERR 0.19-0.21, restored build rc 0, `git diff HEAD` clean | `20..23-*` |
+| maker 20-run arms | XFOLD=0 1/20, XFOLD=1 1/20, both ERR 1.0 | `32-repro-20.txt` |
+| pure-upstream shader path 60-run | **3/60** (this check) | `42-check-upstream-shader-q6k-248320-60.txt` |
+| SX8 same shape/z-split 60-run | **0/60** (this check) | `40-check-sx8-zsplit-60.txt` |
+| DIRECT_SCALES=0 arm, both XFOLD | 43/43 and 43/43 (this check) | `41-check-direct-scales-0-both-xfold.txt` |
+| shader diff | arm 0 is shipped order byte for byte; hoist+fold only under const 4; guard `i < num_blocks_per_row` barrier-free; `sum[k]`↔`xs*` pairing matches shipped `by*` order | `git diff 9ff4644b1 HEAD -- mul_mat_vec_q6_k.comp` |
+| host diff | const 4 passed at both Q6_K dmmv registrations (`:7100`, `:7166`); no `_id` Q6_K dmmv registration exists; MMVQ hatch default `-1` = shipped route | `git diff … ggml-vulkan.cpp` |
+| pairing controls | q4_K / q5_K untouched shaders; their 3 rows below −3% have overlapping triples (q4_K n=2 embd-out B=[10730,9591,10202]; q5_K n=1 gate-up A=[1835,1673,1716] B=[1668,1812,1825]) = noise, correctly reported "NOT filtered" | `32-paired-r48cq6k.txt:101-104` |
+| q6_K rows below −3% | none (16 in route arm, all n≥5 or the n=4 embd-out −12%, as expected for a diagnostic) | `32-paired-r48cq6k*.txt` |
+| route verdict | n≤4 wash/+5% at ffn-down/legacy, n≥5 collapse; default stays f32; R48b hoist may change this later | `32-paired-r48cq6kroute.txt` |
+| registry | `GGML_ARIFI_Q6K_XFOLD`, `GGML_ARIFI_Q6K_MMVQ` rows present (:42-43); `GGML_VK_Q6K_DIRECT_SCALES` :58 | `docs/OPTIONS-REGISTRY.md` |
+| trailers | Origin / Measured-effect / Lane on both `647eb6ac9` and `0e1660a39` | `git log` |
+| stderr receipts | both "direct-scales" and "activation-hoist+xfold" lines present once per run | all receipts |
+
+## NOT CHECKABLE
+
+- Serve-level bit-identity between DIRECT_SCALES arms at XFOLD=1 (needs a model; forbidden here).
+- Report rule 4 (XFOLD=1 vs =0 byte-identical at n≥4, differ at n≤3) — needs a dump harness, not test-backend-ops.
+- The `ggml_vk_synchronize` lead (`ggml-vulkan.cpp:19978-20047`) — read but not tested; belongs to the sync lane.
+- Whether the perf triples for the positive n=6 rows are tight (only rows below −3% print triples).
+
+## VERDICT
+
+Kernel correct in all four constant arms; the intermittent all-zero is proven pre-existing on the
+pure-upstream shader path (3/60) and is Q6_K-path-specific (SX8 0/60 at the same dispatch), so it is not
+this lane's to fix. Pairing: no harm at n=1..5,7,8, +26..+38% at n=6, controls clean. Route hatch
+correctly stays off. Keep, default ON, with two named gates before the lane is called done: (a) rewrite
+the two registry rows with the measured numbers and the "rule 1 not met" statement (findings 5, 6);
+(b) HQ re-runs the protected win's serve-level bit-identity between DIRECT_SCALES arms on the new shader
+(finding 4), and fixes the f16-coverage claim (finding 3).
+
+PASS-GATED (keep, default ON; gates: registry rows rewritten with measured numbers + protected-win serve bit-identity re-run + f16 coverage claim corrected)
